            <ArticleTitle>An update on analgesics for the management of acute postoperative dental pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>476-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acetaminophen, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) and opioids are available as analgesics in dentistry. They each have specific advantages, disadvantages, indications and contraindications. This article provides a brief review of their role in the management of acute postoperative pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
